-- #1904, THE ROUTING DIRECTION: when an enclosing function's own declared context
-- names ONE interface twice at two argument vectors that differ only at NON-LEAD
-- TYVAR positions, the two body occurrences must read TWO DIFFERENT dict slots.
--
-- Hand-derived from DICT-SEMANTICS §3 BEFORE running anything.  `size`'s context is
-- the two 3-ary predicates `Ix a b c` and `Ix a c b`.  The body's first occurrence
-- `ix n x y` has goal `Ix a b c` and the second `ix n y x` has goal `Ix a c b`, so
-- `(d_pi : pi) in P` holds for each with a DIFFERENT pi and (assum) applies twice,
-- to two different assumptions.  At `size 5 'z' True` the instantiation is
-- a=Int, b=Char, c=Bool, so slot 0 is `Ix Int Char Bool` (333) and slot 1 is
-- `Ix Int Bool Char` (111).  The program must print 333 + 111 = 444.
--
-- 🚨 WHAT THIS PINS, AND WHY BOTH HALVES OF #1904 ARE NEEDED FOR IT.  Two
-- independent head-tycon-only encodings had to move before this row could be green:
--   * the KEY (`oblArgKey`, composed into `cslotVecKey`) rendered EVERY tyvar
--     position as the constant "*", so both predicates keyed as `Ix|*,*,*` and
--     `dedupSlotVecs` collapsed them into ONE dict slot -- there was no slot 1 to
--     route to at all;
--   * the ROUTING (`predArgsAgree`/`monoHeadAgrees`, reached from `enclDictVarOf` ->
--     `enclSlotIndex` -> `indexOfPredGo` pass 1) treated a tyvar position as
--     agreeing with EVERYTHING, so even once slot 1 existed both occurrences still
--     matched slot 0 and the new slot was allocated but never read.
-- Fixing only the key widens `size`'s emitted dict arity 4 -> 5 params and changes
-- no answer; fixing only the routing has nothing to route to.
--
-- MEASURED at `44257622` (the merge-base with main) on this tree, cold built:
-- check 0, run 0 and build 0 all printing `666` -- i.e. 333 + 333, the FIRST slot's
-- dict for both occurrences, a silent wrong answer at exit 0 on both engines.
--
-- 🚨 AND IT IS NOT ORDER-DECIDED IN THE USUAL WAY, WHICH IS WHY SECTION 4 IS NOT
-- THE WHOLE GUARD HERE: swapping the two `impl Ix` blocks leaves the base printing
-- `666` too (probes/p1904_both_swap.mdk measured at the same base), because the
-- collapse is to the first CONTEXT SLOT, not to the first IMPL.  Section 4 still
-- grades this file's permutation for free, but the value row above is what sees the
-- defect.
--
-- ⚠️ THE GROUND-POSITION CONTROL is s-multiparam-* / the `(Ix a Char, Ix a Bool)`
-- shape: an identical two-slot context whose slots differ at a GROUND position
-- routes correctly even before #1904, because `monoHeadAgrees` can see a ground
-- head.  A "fix" that only re-ordered slots, or that made pass 1 stricter without
-- the tyvar-identity arm, would move that control and not this row.
interface Ix a b c where
  ix : a -> b -> c -> Int

impl Ix Int Char Bool where
  ix _ _ _ = 333

impl Ix Int Bool Char where
  ix _ _ _ = 111

size : (Ix a b c, Ix a c b) => a -> b -> c -> Int
size n x y = ix n x y + ix n y x

main = println (size 5 'z' True)
